��I think it was the really nice temperatures that started early this year, way back in March. Then it was just a really fertile summer.
That means less stress on the mice, and that means larger litters.��
Kendall Crosby, owner of Kendall��s Ace Hardware Stores in St. Paul, said mousetrap sales are up 30 percent at his two St. Paul locations, when compared with previous several autumns — the traditional time when mice and men meet in basement battle.
