BOSTON — The Red Sox are the heart of Boston, and David Ortiz is the heart of the Red Sox.
The Sox designated hitter had a pair of hits, including the team's only RBI until the eighth inning, in a 4-3 win over the Royals on Saturday. His season debut happened to coincide with the team's first game at Fenway Park following the Marathon explosions.
Ortiz missed the first 15 games of the season and spring training because of right Achilles tendinopathy, and he brought an immediate infusion of charm. That included his choice of words in a pre-game ceremony at Fenway on Saturday.
